$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: A round bottomed flask was charged with
racemic 2,4,6-tribromo-N,N-diisopropyl- 3-methoxybenzamide (4) (236.0 mg,
0.5 mmol), phenyl boronic acid (67.0 mg, 0.55 mmol),
tetrakis(triphenylphosphine)palladium (28.9 mg, 0.025 mmol), and K3PO4
(849.2 mg, 4.0 mmol). The flask was then sealed with a rubber septum and
placed under an inert argon atmosphere. In a 5:1 ratio, degassed THF (4.2
mL) and water (0.83 mL) totaling 0.1 M were then added to the flask. The
reaction was placed in an oil bath and heated at 50 ºC, under Ar, for 20
h. The reaction was then allowed to cool to room temperature and diluted
with ethyl acetate (10 mL). The organics were separated and dried with
sodium sulfate. Purification via reverse phase column chromatography
using a Biotage Isolera system with a KP-C18-HS column (10%
acetonitrile/water to 100% acetonitrile/water; flow rate = 40 mL/min).
The same procedure was carried out utilizing enantioenriched 4 (95:5 er)
on a 0.1 mmol scale (47.2 mg) to obtain 23.6 mg of enantioenriched
product (62% yield). A full characterization of this material was
previously reported, and supports the reported regioisomeric assignment.1
The cross-coupling was also performed on larger scale (1.73 mmol of 4, of
98:2 er). 574.7 mg (81% yield) of 5a with the same enantioenrichment.
This material was then recrystallized from hot diethyl ether/hexanes to
afford material of >99:1 er for further functionalizations (465.3 mg from
two crops of crystals, 81% recovery).
3,5-dibromo-N,N-diisopropyl-2-methoxy-[1,1'-biphenyl]-4-carboxamide (5a).
HPLC 99:1 er (Chiralpak AD-H, 1.0 mL/min, 95:5 hexanes:ethanol):
tR(Minor) = 5.4 min, tR(Major) = 6.8 min; [α] 20.0 D – 7.5 (c 1.0,
CHCl3); 1H NMR (500 MHz, MeOD) δ 7.61 (s, 1H), 7.96 – 7.53 (m, 2H), 7.50
– 7.44 (m, 2H), 7.44 – 7.39 (m, 1H), 3.76 – 3.64 (m, 2H), 3.42 (s, 3H),
1.61 (d, J = 6.8 Hz, 3H), 1.60 (d, J = 6.8 Hz, 3H), 1.31 (d, J = 6.6 Hz,
6H); HRMS (FT-ICR, ESI) m/z calculated for C20H24Br2NO2 + [M+H]+
470.0149, found 470.0138.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM regioselective, stereoselective, other products also detected, sealed
tube used, Suzuki-Miyaura cross-coupling reaction
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Regioselective Derivatizations of a Tribrominated Atropisomeric Benzamide
Scaffold
