$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM tert-butyl((1Z,4E)-4-methyl-2-phenyl-5-(trimethylsilyl)penta-1,4-dien-1-yl)carbamate
(7). A microwave vial was charged with alkene (3d) (39.5 mg, 0.1 mmol, 1
equiv.), iodobenzene (40.8 mg, 0.2 mmol, 2 equiv.), DME (0.33 mL), and
H2O (0.17 mL). The solution was degassed by bubbling argon through the
mixture for 10 minutes. The vial was quickly opened and Pd(dppf)Cl2 (5.8
mg, 0.05 mmol, 0.05 equiv.) and NaHCO3 (33.6 mg, 0.4 mmol, 4 equiv.) were
added. The resulting heterogeneous solution was degassed for an
additional 10 minutes after which it was sealed and heated at 85 °C for
8h. The solution was then allowed to cool to room temperature at which
time it was diluted with ethyl acetate (3 mL). The organic layer was
removed and the remaining aqueous phase was extracted with ethyl acetate
(2 X 3 mL). The organic fractions were combined, passed through a small
plug of silica, and evaporated. The crude oil was purified by column
chromatography, eluting with 3% ethyl acetate:pet ether. The product (26
mg, 75% yield) as a colorless oil. Rf: 0.41 (5% ethyl acetate:pet ether)
(KMNO4, UV). 1H NMR (500 MHz; CDCl3): δ 7.45 (t, J = 7.2, 2H), 7.36-7.33
(m, 1H), 7.27 (d, J = 7.3, 2H), 6.68 (d, J = 11.4, 1H), 6.38 (d, J =
10.7, 1H), 5.24 (s, 1H), 3.13 (s, 2H), 1.82 (s, 3H), 1.53 (s, 9H), 0.10
(s, 9H). 80 °C Toluene: 1H NMR (500 MHz; toluene): δ 7.05-6.93
(Overlapping phenyl ring and toluene solvent signal), 6.76 (d, J = 11.3,
1H), 6.17 (bs, 1H), 5.22 (s, 1H), 2.95 (s, 2H), 1.68 (s, 3H), 1.31 (s,
9H), 0.03 (s, 9H) 13C NMR (125 MHz; CDCl3): δ 152.95, 152.08, 138.66,
128.87. 128.48, 127.03, 126.49, 121.16, 118.07, 80.58, 49.58, 28.40,
21.23, 0.03 IR (thin film): 3392, 2913, 1705, 1643, 1458, 1348, 1230,
1144, 855 cm-1. NOE: Irradiation of H1~12.4% H3, Irradiation of H1~ 12.8%
H2 HRMS (ESI+) calcd for [M+Na]+ C20H31NaNO2Si+ 368.2022, Found 368.2008.
